Title: "Overview"
Id: "8be9eb88-9a8e-48d3-99d3-7f80bf78cf15"

Text: "Forms describe the shape of notation rather than a concrete value.

Forms are used in command headers, described targets, alias left-hand sides, and declarations. Common form shapes are:

```mlg-fragment
x
x_
x__
f(x_)
f(x__)
(x_, y_)
{x_ : ...}
G ::= (X, *, e)
```

A form can introduce symbols when it appears in a declaration position. For
example, `G ::= (X, *, e)` introduces `G`, `X`, `*`, and `e` as symbols whose
roles must be specified by the surrounding declaration."
Id: "796fefea-e968-4ebc-8538-be43b9f88b2b"
